  "issuedISO": "2026-11-27T15:34:00-10:00",
  "discussion": "An extra large north-northwest (330 to 350 degree) swell has been gradually fading today, and a high surf advisory for north facing shores of all islands is now in place through tonight. The west facing shores were dropped from an advisory due to the fact that as the northwest swell has been declining, the swell has been becoming more northerly. The swell will fade further through the weekend, with surf dropping below advisory levels on Saturday. A small to moderate northwest swell arrives late Sunday and peaks on Monday, then fades through mid-week. A larger long period northwest swell follows this, arriving Wednesday and peaking in the latter half of next week. Surf heights along east-facing shores will continue to be elevated tonight due to wrapping from the north-northwest swell. As the swell fades, a medium-period northeast swell generated by a storm- force low to the northeast of the islands will keep surf elevated for east- facing shores through Sunday. More typical, short- period trade wind swell will return by Monday. Surf along south- facing shores will remain tiny to small tonight, with a small bump possible this Saturday through Sunday, followed by a return to background small to flat levels next week.",
